  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Reported commands use 'told + person + to + verb' for positive commands, and 'told + person + not to + verb' for negative commands: 'Close the door' → 'She told me to close the door.' 'Don't be late' → 'He told me not to be late.'",
    "explanation_ko": "간접화법 명령문은 긍정 명령에는 'told + 사람 + to + 동사', 부정 명령에는 'told + 사람 + not to + 동사'를 씁니다: 'Close the door' → 'She told me to close the door.' 'Don't be late' → 'He told me not to be late.'",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "The doctor told me to rest for a week.",
        "ko": "의사는 저에게 일주일 쉬라고 했어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "My boss told me not to worry about it.",
        "ko": "제 상사는 걱정하지 말라고 했어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "She told us to be quiet.",
        "ko": "그녀는 우리에게 조용히 하라고 했어요."
      }
    ]
  },
